  "final_message": "Customers with no payment method now go through dunning. The 24 existing tests pass. I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case.\n\n**Root cause:** in `collect` (`billing/payments.py`), when `default_payment_method` returned `None`, the function returned immediately without calling `record_failure`. The expired-card and gateway-failure paths both call it. So with no payment method, nothing incremented `attempt_count`, no `invoice.payment_failed` event was emitted, no `next_attempt_at` was scheduled, and the subscription never moved to `past_due`.\n\n**Fix:** that branch now calls `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")` before returning `None`. The failure code `\"no_payment_method\"` is my choice, so rename it if you have a convention.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` as `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
